    <paragraph>Use the Discriminant to Predict the Number of Real Solutions of a Quadratic Equation</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, determine the number of real solutions for each quadratic equation.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="145" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$4x^{2} - 5x + 16 = 0$$ ⓑ $$36y^{2} + 36y + 9 = 0$$ ⓒ $$6m^{2} + 3m - 5 = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$no real solutionsno real solutions$$ ⓑ $$11$$ ⓒ $$22$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="146" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$9v^{2} - 15v + 25 = 0$$ ⓑ $$100w^{2} + 60w + 9 = 0$$ ⓒ $$5c^{2} + 7c - 10 = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="147" has_solution="true">
